		(uuid "84ab7502-ae50-430f-81fb-9ad460664c84")
	)
	(text "U1201 (TPS568215RNNR) converts FPGA5V5 into the core supply.\nCMD_CORE drives Q1201; R1201 (100 kOhm) pulls EN_CORE low.\nThe source follower allows enable only with the input rail available;\nthe command driver must provide a defined state and enough EN margin.\nC1201/C1202 (47 uF each) and C1204 (100 nF) bypass the input."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 156.21 65.3 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.55 1.55)
				(thickness 0.15)
				(color 33 43 55 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8f2bcce4-33c5-43f7-b331-b43a8be3921d")
	)
	(text "Input and enable"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 156.21 60.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.9 1.9)
				(thickness 0.18)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 100 110 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "93afd1da-d6c3-48ec-a34a-9d314bbfcc97")
	)
	(text "FB senses CORE_RAW.\nR1205: 2 mV drop per ampere."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 101 136.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.15 1.15)
				(thickness 0.15)
				(color 0 70 190 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "940d5da6-a98e-43e8-b188-a6ff0c2d14e9")
	)
	(text "R1203 (10.2 kOhm) and R1204 (15 kOhm) set FB_CORE from CORE_RAW:\nV(CORE_RAW) = 0.6 V x (1 + R1203 / R1204) = 1.008 V.\nIncreasing R1203 raises the voltage; increasing R1204 lowers it.\nFor another setting: R1203 = R1204 x (VOUT / 0.6 V - 1).\nChoose the setting within the selected FPGA core voltage limits."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 156.21 116 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.55 1.55)
				(thickness 0.15)
				(color 33 43 55 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "94806be4-e9fb-4235-8d3c-e5c880762b1b")
	)
	(text "200 kOhm / 10 kOhm:\n400 kHz, FCCM, ILIM."
